@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# U-Boot environment location on the Anpviz / MC-A85 (OEM LX510 U-Boot).
+#
+# Deliberately a FILE, not flash. This OEM U-Boot keeps its saveenv copy at
+# flash 0x30000 -- the first block of the kernel partition (mtd1) -- and
+# thingino's default "/dev/mtd1 0x0" pointed straight at it, so every
+# fw_setenv (S97sysupgrade's "mark sysupgrade complete", the WebUI) erased the
+# kernel's first 64 KB and the next boot failed with "Wrong Image Format".
+# U-Boot boots from its built-in bootargs, so nothing needs to reach its env
+# from Linux; fw_setenv/fw_printenv work against this scratch file instead.
+#
+# <device> <offset> <env size>
+/etc/fw_env.dat 0x0 0x10000
